<spell-notebook "section theming">
	<header level="1">
		Section
		<header>A section is a titled block of content that can close and keep its title in view.</>
	</>
	<section-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
			<item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
			<item link="#themes">Themes</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme with the public `--ui-section-*` tokens:
			set one on the element, on any ancestor (`:root` for every section), or on the box through `::part(section)`.

			- the `basic` look replaces the box, rule and tint, whatever you set.
			- Never set the `--_ui-section-*` names:  they're the sheet's private plumbing.

			Style the pieces with `::part()`:

			- `title`:  the bar that sticks;  in it, `heading`, and with `collapsible`, `toggle` and `fold-icon`
			- `icon`, `header` (the title's text), `badge`, `actions`
			- `tip`:  the `description`, under the title bar
			- `subhead`:  the hint
			- `content`
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			ui-section {
			  --ui-section-scrolling-height: 20em;
			  /* chevron up while open, down while closed */
			  --ui-section-fold-icon-rotate: 180deg;
			  --ui-section-fold-icon-folded-rotate: 0deg;
			}
			ui-section::part(heading) {
			  letter-spacing: 0.02em;
			}
			```
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-section" playground>
				<ui-section label="Getting started">
					<ui-text paragraph>A titled block of content. Its title is a real heading: an <ui-text code>h2</> at the top level.</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			Section is ours, not Fomantic's:  the theme menu in the header changes the page around it, and the
			header, segment and accordion looks it borrows follow the colour scheme.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
